# Copyright (c) d-SEAMS developers
# Bounds that stop a hostile file from crashing or hanging a reader
# chemfiles already ships, and the SQLite3 dependency of the
# installed package.
#   TextFile keeps the file position right after its line buffer grows
#   (every later step offset was wrong) and no longer reads a NUL first
#   byte as "buffer empty"; SMI stops at EOF.
#   BinaryFile checks reads and skips against the bytes left in the file;
#   XDR, XTC, TRR, TPR, DCD and Amber NetCDF check their counts, sizes,
#   indices and compressed-coordinate bit widths against it, and TPR
#   checks each function type before renumbering it.
#   CSSR checks atom and bond ids, GRO rejects a box GROMACS cannot hold
#   instead of asserting, LAMMPS Data checks its atom count and sections,
#   LAMMPS trajectories check the box bounds, the atom count and each
#   atom id instead of asserting, TNG holds its frame-scan block-id buffer
#   in TngBuffer<int64_t> and reads a frame's positions before it
#   allocates the frame's atoms, a TRR frame with atoms but no positions,
#   velocities or forces is an error (nothing ties its atom count to the
#   file), an SMI square brace must hold an atom, the extended XYZ comment
#   parser stops at an '=' with no name before it instead of looping, PDB
#   CONECT records are ignored with a warning when no atoms have been read
#   yet, MMTF atom_id checks atom indices and model offsets with
#   FormatError instead of assert(), and S_ISREG is defined where the C
#   library lacks it (MSVC).
